---
import ProseLayout from '@/layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
---

<ProseLayout
  eyebrow="Corrections"
  title="How we correct the record"
  description="How Runtime Signals handles factual errors, material updates, and retired pieces."
  canonicalPath="/corrections"
>
  <p>
    When a published claim turns out to be wrong, outdated, or missing an important limitation, we
    fix it in place. The article keeps its URL. The fix carries a visible revision note and an
    updated timestamp, and the original claim is never quietly edited away.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every revision, correction or not, is recorded on the article itself under "Revision history"
    with one of these badges, exactly as they appear there:
  </p>

  <ul class="badge-key">
    <li>
      <span class="revision-badge" data-type="published">published</span>
      <span>The original approved publication.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="revision-badge" data-type="update">update</span>
      <span>A routine content or dependency fix.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="revision-badge" data-type="correction">correction</span>
      <span>A factual error, fixed and disclosed.</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    See, for example, <a
      href="/articles/model-handoff-as-distributed-state-transfer#revision-history"
      >the revision history on our handoff piece</a
    >. When a factual correction is needed, it carries a visible notice at the top of the article,
    not just an entry at the bottom.
  </p>

  <div class="corrections-contact">
    <p class="corrections-contact__title">Found a factual error?</p>
    <p class="corrections-contact__copy">
      Email <a
        href="mailto:care@runtimesignals.tech?subject=Correction%20request%20-%20Runtime%20Signals"
        >care@runtimesignals.tech</a
      > with the article URL, the claim ID in question, and supporting primary evidence.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Retiring a piece - because a tool it covers no longer exists, or its practice no longer holds -
    is a separate action from a correction. Retired pieces are marked archived, stay reachable at
    their original URL with a notice, and drop out of the active feed and search index.
  </p>
  <p>
    No article moves in either direction without human review; a routine content or dependency fix
    does not require the same review a factual correction does, but neither is automated end to end.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>

<style>
  .badge-key {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-5) 0;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .badge-key li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .badge-key li:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .revision-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.15em 0.5em;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .revision-badge[data-type='correction'] {
    color: var(--evidence-mixed);
  }

  .revision-badge[data-type='update'] {
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  .revision-badge[data-type='published'] {
    color: var(--evidence-supported);
  }

  .corrections-contact {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .corrections-contact__title {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .corrections-contact__copy {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }
</style>
